  (:NAME "ASSERT" :KIND :MACRO :LAMBDA-LIST "(test-form &optional places datum &rest arguments)" :DOCSTRING "Signals an error if the value of TEST-FORM is NIL. Returns NIL.

Optional DATUM and ARGUMENTS can be used to change the signaled
error condition and are interpreted as in (APPLY #'ERROR DATUM
ARGUMENTS).

Continuing from the signaled error using the CONTINUE restart will
allow the user to alter the values of the SETFable locations
specified in PLACES and then start over with TEST-FORM.

If TEST-FORM is of the form

  (FUNCTION ARG*)

where FUNCTION is a function (but not a special operator like
CL:OR, CL:AND, etc.) the results of evaluating the ARGs will be
included in the error report if the assertion fails." :ORIGIN :SBCL :CLHS-PAGE "Body/m_assert.htm")
  (:NAME "ASSOC" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(item alist &key key (test nil testp) (test-not nil notp))" :DOCSTRING "Return the cons in ALIST whose car is equal (by a given test or EQL) to
the ITEM." :ORIGIN :SBCL :CLHS-PAGE "Body/f_assocc.htm")
  (:NAME "ASSOC-IF" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(predicate alist &key key)" :DOCSTRING "Return the first cons in ALIST whose CAR satisfies PREDICATE. If
KEY is supplied, apply it to the CAR of each cons before testing." :ORIGIN :SBCL :CLHS-PAGE "Body/f_assocc.htm")
  (:NAME "ASSOC-IF-NOT" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(predicate alist &key key)" :DOCSTRING "Return the first cons in ALIST whose CAR does not satisfy PREDICATE.
If KEY is supplied, apply it to the CAR of each cons before testing." :ORIGIN :SBCL :CLHS-PAGE "Body/f_assocc.htm")
  (:NAME "ATAN" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(y &optional (x nil xp))" :DOCSTRING "Return the arc tangent of Y if X is omitted or Y/X if X is supplied." :ORIGIN :SBCL :CLHS-PAGE "Body/f_asin_.htm")
  (:NAME "ATANH" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(number)" :DOCSTRING "Return the hyperbolic arc tangent of NUMBER." :ORIGIN :SBCL :CLHS-PAGE "Body/f_sinh_.htm")
  (:NAME "ATOM" :KIND :FUNCTION :LAMBDA-LIST "(object)" :DOCSTRING "Return true if OBJECT is an ATOM, and NIL otherwise." :ORIGIN :SBCL :CLHS-PAGE "Body/a_atom.htm")
